---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { COMPANY, TICKET_REFUND_DAYS } from '../../lib/company';

const mail = `mailto:${COMPANY.email}`;
---

<LegalPage title="Terms of sale" description={`Terms for buying merch and tickets from ${COMPANY.registeredName}.`}>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you buy merch or tickets on this website. Please read them before you buy — by placing an
    order you agree to them. They don't affect your statutory rights as a consumer.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website is run by <strong>{COMPANY.registeredName}</strong>, a company registered in {COMPANY.registeredIn}{" "}
    (company number {COMPANY.registeredNumber}). Registered office: {COMPANY.registeredOffice}. Email:{" "}
    <a href={mail}>{COMPANY.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices are shown in pounds sterling (or the currency shown next to the price) and are the total you pay.</li>
    <li>
      {COMPANY.registeredName} is not registered for VAT, so no VAT is charged.
    </li>
    <li>Merch prices include delivery. Ticket prices include all fees — there's nothing added at checkout.</li>
    <li>
      Payments are processed securely by Stripe. We never see or store your full card details. Your order is
      confirmed when payment succeeds and you see the confirmation page.
    </li>
    <li>
      If we make an obvious pricing mistake, we'll contact you and you can choose to go ahead at the correct price or
      get a full refund.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Merch</h2>

  <h3>Delivery</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>We ship to the countries offered at checkout. We'll dispatch your order within 30 days.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Orders outside the UK:</strong> your country may charge import duties, taxes or handling fees when the
      parcel arrives. These are set by your country, aren't included in our prices, and are your responsibility.
    </li>
    <li>If your order hasn't arrived within a reasonable time, email us and we'll help.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Changing your mind (14 days)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can cancel your merch order for any reason within <strong>14 days of the day you receive it</strong>. Tell
      us by email at <a href={mail}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with your order reference.
    </li>
    <li>
      You then have a further <strong>14 days</strong> to send the item back. <strong>You pay the return postage</strong>,
      and we recommend a tracked service, as the item is your responsibility until it reaches us.
    </li>
    <li>
      We'll refund the price you paid (including the original delivery, which is built into the price) within 14 days
      of receiving the item back, or of you showing proof you posted it — whichever is sooner — to your original
      payment method.
    </li>
    <li>
      Items should come back unused and in the condition you received them. If an item has been handled more than
      needed to check it (for example worn or washed), we may reduce the refund to reflect the loss in value.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Faulty or wrong items</h3>
  <p>
    If something arrives faulty, damaged or not as described, email us. Under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 you can
    reject it for a full refund within 30 days of delivery; after that you're entitled to a repair or replacement,
    and a refund if that doesn't fix it. For faulty or wrong items, we cover the cost of returning them.
  </p>

  <h2>Tickets for our shows</h2>
  <p>These terms only apply to tickets for shows we run and sell tickets for on this website.</p>

  <h3>Your ticket</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      When your payment succeeds, your name goes on the door list for that show. Bring your confirmation email (or the
      card you paid with) and we'll check you in at the door.
    </li>
    <li>
      Age limits and entry requirements vary by show and are shown on the listing. You may be asked for ID. If you
      don't meet a show's entry requirements, you may be refused entry and won't be entitled to a refund.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Refunds if you can't come</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Because tickets are for an event on a specific date, the usual 14-day right to cancel online purchases 
      <strong> does not apply to tickets</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Instead, you can get a <strong>full refund if you ask at least {TICKET_REFUND_DAYS} days before the show</strong>.
      Email <a href={mail}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with your order reference. Refunds go back to your original payment
      method.
    </li>
    <li>Less than {TICKET_REFUND_DAYS} days before the show, tickets can't be refunded.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>If we cancel or move a show</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      If we cancel a show, you can choose either a <strong>full refund</strong> or to use your ticket for the
      <strong> next show we run in the same city</strong>. We'll email you to ask which you'd prefer.
    </li>
    <li>
      If we move a show to a new date, your ticket is valid for the new date. If you can't make the new date, you can
      ask for a full refund.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Tickets for other promoters' shows</h3>
  <p>
    Some listings link to another company's ticket site. Those tickets are sold by that company under its own terms,
    not by us.
  </p>

  <h2>Our responsibility to you</h2>
  <p>
    We're responsible for loss or damage you suffer that's a foreseeable result of us breaking these terms or failing
    to use reasonable care and skill. We're not responsible for loss that isn't foreseeable, or for events outside our
    reasonable control. Nothing in these terms limits our liability where it would be unlawful to do so, including
    for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, or for fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={mail}>{COMPANY.email}</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can. These terms are governed by
    the law of {COMPANY.registeredIn}. If you live elsewhere in the UK, you can also bring proceedings in your local
    courts.
  </p>

  <p>See also our <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
